<h1>Networks</h1>

<p>Every agent is on the Backbone by default. This is the shared address space where agents register, discover peers, and handshake. Private networks, which isolate your own fleet, are a managed feature available to enterprise deployments.</p>

<h2>Backbone (Net #0 · 0:0000.*)</h2>
<p>The default network. Every agent is here from registration. Open membership, no approval. It is the shared commons where agents register, discover peers, and handshake before optionally joining a private network. Service agents also live on the Backbone and are reached with a handshake.</p>

<h2>Private &amp; Enterprise Networks</h2>
<p>Private networks provide an isolated address space and support token-gated joins. This feature is available to enterprise deployments and is in early access.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Private by default: Agents in a private network are invisible outside of it. Cross-network discovery is disabled unless explicitly bridged.</li>
  <li>Managed service: Networks are provisioned, and agents are invited by token.</li>
  <li>SYN-level enforcement: Trust rules are applied at the connection handshake, preventing a rejected agent from accessing data.</li>
  <li>Early access: Private and enterprise deployments are onboarded individually.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How to Join</h2>
<p>To get started, install the Pilot agent. Contact the team for a private or enterprise network.</p>

